# ICN Jobs Literature Review — Index

Master catalog of all wiki pages and their relationships. Populated automatically after ingest.

## Studies

Key research studies and reports:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[ferdman-2026-ai-deskilling-structural-problem]] | 2026-07-10 | 2026-09-26 | Avigail Ferdman's 2026 paper in AI & Society presenting a structural analysis of how AI systems can undermine human capacities through systemic environmental conditions rather than individual failings. Introduces the critical distinction between capacity-hostile and capacity-conducive environments, analyzes the role of agential control and habituation in capacity development, and examines how Artificial Personal Assistants may create capacity-hostile environments by encouraging plan-following rather than plan-forming. The paper argues that deskilling should be understood as a structural problem requiring societal solutions rather than merely an individual responsibility issue. Expanded with detailed analysis of methodology, key findings, market research implications, specific examples, and evaluation frameworks for AI tools. |

## Concepts

Cross-cutting ideas, trends, and frameworks:

| Page | Description |
|------|-------------|
| [[capacity-hostile-environments]] | Environments that restrict, limit, or create a narrow field of affordances for capacity development and exercise, often encouraged by AI automation. |
| [[capacity-conducive-environments]] | Environments that afford opportunities for cultivating core human capacities, encouraging agential control and embodied habituation. |
| [[agential-control]] | The ability to adjust action execution and initiate tasks purposefully, distinguishing skills from habits. |
| [[habituation]] | Gradual process of becoming skilled through practice, learning from mistakes, and embodied/intersubjective engagement. |
| [[affordances]] | Action possibilities formed by the relationship between an agent and its environment; invitations that influence behavior. |
| [[developmental-perfectionism]] | Neo-Aristotelian approach defining flourishing as competent exercise of core human capacities yielding intrinsic value. |
| [[arts-of-personhood]] | Epistemic, social, moral, and creative capacities required for practical reason, self-worth, and mutual respect. |
| [[field-of-affordances]] | Range of action possibilities available in an environment; narrow fields risk affordance shrinkage and deskilling. |
| [[plan-following-vs-plan-forming]] | Distinction between responding to AI recommendations (habitual) and initiating/coordination plans (agential). |

## Skills

Skills, competencies, and requirements:

| Page | Description |
|------|-------------|
| [[epistemic-capacities]] | Theoretical and practical rationality required for knowledge acquisition, critical reflection, and wise decision-making. |
| [[social-capacities]] | Moral and caring capacities for developing meaningful relationships, coordination, and shared valuing. |
| [[creative-capacity]] | Ability to make unfamiliar combinations of ideas, transform conceptual space, and generate novel solutions. |
| [[volitional-capacity]] | Meta-capacity enabling effort, perseverance, and growth to achieve intrinsically valuable goals. |
| [[practical-wisdom]] | Phronesis; real-world experience, discernment, and effective navigation of complex circumstances. |

